{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"orthogonal-demoniac-kusimanse","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Purpose\nThis ticket is the mechanism-ratchet admission for the `.append.lock` sibling lock in `src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py` (kind `lock`, name `.append.lock`). Every alert appender serializes on that dotfile through `rebar._store.fsutil.sibling_exclusive_lock`. It replaced an in-file fcntl flock that Windows lacks (appends there overwrote each other), and it is permanent: the store's portable lock kernel is the only append serialization that works on every supported platform. Delivered by charitable-tyrannical-hydra (b8dd-85be-1dbb-45b9).\n\nThe repo has one convention for admitting a mechanism added after the baseline froze (`docs/architecture.md` §\"Mechanism-delta ratchet\"; `src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py`). A `# mechanism-ok:` marker at the definition site names a ticket, and rebar refuses to close that ticket while the marker remains. The marker above `_APPEND_LOCK_NAME` names this ticket. Precedents: added-ephemeral-seaslug, unpleasing-starchy-teal.\n\n## Lifecycle\n- This ticket stays `open` and unclaimed as long as the `.append.lock` sibling exists. Do not work it and do not close it.\n- It closes only when a future change removes that lock. That change deletes the marker in the same commit and runs `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale`.","id":"3bc8-49a4-6c84-4b19","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Keep alert_store .append.lock admitted (permanent; stays open while the lock exists)"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795360076331411001,"uuid":"8e8104ed-af58-420d-97e8-5ceb4ee07964"}